---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Mark from '../components/Mark.astro';

const ASK = 'https://github.com/cookc/steadyship/issues/new?title=I%20want%3A%20&body=What%20would%20you%20want%20Steadyship%20to%20do%20first%2C%20and%20for%20what%20kind%20of%20business%3F';

const brings = [
  {
    title: 'Asks what you don\'t know to ask',
    icon: '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9.5 9a2.5 2.5 0 1 1 3.5 2.3c-.7.4-1 1-1 1.7"/><path d="M12 17h.01"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg>',
    body: 'Before a change is built, it has read your business notes, your other apps and your spreadsheets. So it asks the one or two questions that would be expensive to get wrong, recommends an answer, and builds once you decide.',
    example: 'You say "Make the job board track hours." It asks: against the whole job, or each step? And isn\'t that already in Hours.csv on the shared drive?',
  },
  {
    title: 'Judges what you can\'t judge',
    icon: '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 5-3.5 8.5-8 9-4.5-.5-8-4-8-9V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg>',
    body: 'A straight Yes, No or Not yet on whether the team can rely on an app, with the evidence. Security in plain words: who can see this, where what people type ends up, whether a password is sitting in a file.',
    example: 'It never calls an app secure. It says what it checked, and labels what it could not.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Brings engineering when it\'s needed, not before',
    icon: '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 20V10M10 20V4M16 20v-8M22 20H2"/></svg>',
    body: 'A prototype stays a prototype. The day someone relies on it, it gets one master for its data, a backup, a test, a named owner and its decisions written down, each step with one plain line on why. The apps stop drifting apart.',
    example: 'A one-person tool gets no ceremony. The day the workshop runs on it, it gets looked after like software.',
  },
];

const features = [
  { title: 'Asks before it builds', body: 'The one or two questions that would be expensive to get wrong, with a recommendation. You decide, it builds, and it writes down why.' },
  { title: 'Gives a straight verdict', body: 'Yes, No or Not yet on whether the team can rely on an app, with the evidence. A second reviewer checks the first.' },
  { title: 'Finds the same thing kept twice', body: 'Reads every app and every spreadsheet and shows where a price, a job or a name is in two places and already disagrees.' },
  { title: 'Checks the ground first', body: 'Can it reach GitHub, read and write the shared drive, open your app? One minute, PASS or FAIL, written down.' },
  { title: 'A path, not a rebuild', body: 'Prototype, owned tool, proper app, platform. It says which stage an app is at and moves it one step at a time, with you deciding at each.' },
  { title: 'Apps that stay in step', body: 'A shared glossary with a human owner. Every app reading the same spreadsheets instead of its own copy.' },
  { title: 'A second opinion from another vendor', body: 'A reviewer from a different AI vendor, so it does not share the builder\'s blind spots. No terminal needed.' },
  { title: 'Everything stays yours', body: 'Ordinary files in a private folder the business owns. Remove it tomorrow and everything it wrote is still there.' },
];

const stages = [
  { name: 'Prototype', looks: 'One file, one person\'s tool.', trigger: 'someone else starts using it.' },
  { name: 'Owned tool', looks: 'Shared, backed-up data with one writer. A test. A named owner.', trigger: 'two apps touch the same information.' },
  { name: 'Proper app', looks: 'A real framework, shared parts, data checked on the way in.', trigger: 'the business depends on it daily.' },
  { name: 'Platform', looks: 'Several apps on one database, kept in step.', trigger: 'they must stay consistent for the business to run.' },
];

const steps = [
  { prompt: 'Set up Steadyship for Harbour Boatworks', note: 'Answer four questions. About two minutes.' },
  { prompt: 'Check this computer', note: 'Three checks, one minute, recorded.' },
  { prompt: 'Review the job board', note: 'A verdict the owner can act on.' },
];
---
<Base title="Steadyship" description="An engineer in the conversation. A Claude plugin for businesses whose own people build their apps: it asks what you don't know to ask, judges what you can't judge, and brings in real engineering the moment an app starts to matter.">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-16 pt-16 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-12 md:grid-cols-[1.2fr_1fr]">
      <div>
        <p class="font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sea">A plugin for Claude</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl font-extrabold leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">An engineer in the conversation.</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
          Your team builds its own apps with Claude. Steadyship is the engineer working beside them, always:
          it asks what they don't know to ask, judges what they can't judge, and brings in real engineering the
          moment an app starts to matter. Not before.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="/get-started" class="rounded-full bg-navy px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-sea">Get started</a>
          <a href="/features" class="rounded-full border border-[var(--line)] px-6 py-3 font-semibold hover:border-sea">See what it does</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--muted)]">Open source. Stays on your computer. Keeps working if you remove it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-center md:justify-end">
        <Mark size={260} class="drop-shadow-[0_24px_40px_rgba(17,49,79,0.25)]" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What an engineer brings -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pb-20 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What an engineer brings</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[var(--muted)]">Claude builds what it is asked to build. These are the three things nobody in the building was there to add.</p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {brings.map((b) => (
        <article class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] p-6">
          <div class="flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-sea/10 text-sea" set:html={b.icon} />
          <h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-xl font-bold">{b.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">{b.body}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">{b.example}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Features -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--surface)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">What it does</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[var(--muted)]">Each one is a plain sentence in Claude. No dashboard, no account, nothing to learn. Everything it finds goes into files you keep.</p>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {features.map((c, i) => (
          <article class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--bg)] p-6">
            <span class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-sea">0{i + 1}</span>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-bold">{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">{c.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <a href="/features" class="font-semibold text-sea hover:underline">All of it, in more detail</a>
        <span class="text-[var(--muted)]">·</span>
        <a href={ASK} class="font-semibold text-sea hover:underline">Tell us which one you'd want first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">How it works</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[var(--muted)]">Three sentences on day one. After that, ask for changes the way you already do.</p>
    <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {steps.map((s, i) => (
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] p-6">
          <span class="inline-flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-sea font-display text-sm font-bold text-white">{i + 1}</span>
          <p class="mt-4 rounded-xl bg-[var(--surface)] px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm">“{s.prompt}”</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] text-[var(--muted)]">{s.note}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- See it answer -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--surface)]">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-start gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_1.2fr]">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">See it answer</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed">
          A real reply from the demo business, a boat builder with six apps its staff built with Claude.
          The short version is what you read. The full picture, every row that differs, goes into a file you keep.
        </p>
        <a href="/get-started" class="mt-6 inline-block font-semibold text-sea hover:underline">Try it on the demo business</a>
      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed">
        <div class="bubble-user ml-auto max-w-md px-5 py-3">What apps do we have and where is the same information kept twice?</div>
        <div class="bubble-reply px-5 py-4">
          <p class="font-semibold">The three things that matter most</p>
          <ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5">
            <li><strong>The Quote Builder is using old prices.</strong> Price List 2026.csv has Bimini top $3,450 and Trailer $6,250. The app has $3,200 and $5,800, so a quote with both is $700 low before GST.</li>
            <li><strong>The job list is typed into several places, and they disagree.</strong> Jobs.csv has 8 jobs. Job Board has 8, Delivery Checklist 4 and Shop Timer 3. J-1039 is “Sea trial” in Jobs.csv but “Paint” on the board.</li>
            <li><strong>If a laptop died, most of the work would be lost.</strong> Five apps keep what people enter only in that browser on that computer.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="mt-3 font-semibold">What I'd do first</p>
          <p class="mt-1">Update the Quote Builder's two prices, and make it read Price List 2026.csv. It is the one customers see numbers from.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--muted)]">The full picture is in docs/assessment/SUMMARY.md. Say ‘show me everything’ and I'll put it here.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The path -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">From prototype to something the business runs on</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
      Every app is at one of four stages. Steadyship says which, what would move it on, and does the moving one step
      at a time with a review at each step. Nobody has to choose a framework, a database or a host. It makes the call,
      gives the reason, and you can defer.
    </p>
    <ol class="mt-10 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-4">
      {stages.map((st, i) => (
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] p-5">
          <span class="font-display text-sm font-bold text-sea">Stage {i + 1}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-1 font-display text-lg font-bold">{st.name}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">{st.looks}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-[14px] leading-relaxed"><span class="font-semibold">Moves on when</span> {st.trigger}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl bg-navy p-6 text-white dark:bg-sea-deep md:flex md:items-center md:justify-between md:gap-8">
      <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#C6D3DE]">
        <span class="font-display font-bold text-white">Always there, never in the way.</span>{" "}
        Exploring? Prototype as you do today; it asks at most once and never blocks. Keeping it? It gets a name, an owner and a first verdict.
        Relying on it? The stages run, with you deciding at each. Short answers, with more if you ask.
      </p>
      <a href="/features" class="mt-4 inline-block shrink-0 font-semibold text-sun hover:underline md:mt-0">How each step works</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Who it's for -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--surface)]">
    <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Who it's for</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
          A business where a few people who are not developers build their own tools with Claude, and those tools are
          starting to matter. A job board someone relies on. A quote builder that disagrees with the price list.
          Two apps that both keep the customer list.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
          One person does a ten-minute setup. The owner decides what the business relies on. Everyone else keeps building,
          with an engineer in the conversation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--bg)] p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-bold">What it is not</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
          <li>Not a place to host apps, and not a database.</li>
          <li>Not a replacement for Claude. It sits in the same chat.</li>
          <li>Not a certificate that an app is secure. It tells you what it checked and what it could not.</li>
          <li>Not in the way. It stays quiet until something matters.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-20 pb-8 sm:px-6">
    <div class="rounded-3xl bg-navy px-6 py-12 text-center text-white dark:border dark:border-white/10 sm:px-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold">Ten minutes to a first verdict.</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-[#C6D3DE]">Windows or Mac, the Claude desktop app or Claude Code in a terminal. One page for each.</p>
      <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="/get-started" class="inline-block rounded-full bg-sun px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-navy hover:bg-[#F7C95F]">Get started</a>
        <a href={ASK} class="inline-block rounded-full border border-white/30 px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:border-white">Tell us what you'd want first</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
